  "pformat": "<document source=\"test/functional/input/latex_literal_block.rst\">\n    <paragraph>\n        In LaTeX, literal blocks can be customized with the \"literal-block-env\"\n        setting. This test file exists to check if the LaTeX writer output compiles\n        and looks as expected.\n    <paragraph>\n        Start with a plain literal block:\n    <literal_block xml:space=\"preserve\">\n        $\\sin^2(x)$ and $\\cos^2(x)$ equals one:\n        \n        \\[\n           \\sin^2(x) + \\cos^2(x) = 1 % for all x\n        \\]\n    <paragraph>\n        A latex \"code-block\" (set with \"literal-block-env\", if syntax\n        highlight is \"none\"):\n    <system_message level=\"2\" line=\"16\" source=\"test/functional/input/latex_literal_block.rst\" type=\"WARNING\">\n        <paragraph>\n            Cannot analyze code. Pygments package not found.\n        <literal_block xml:space=\"preserve\">\n            .. code:: latex\n            \n              $\\sin^2(x)$ and $\\cos^2(x)$ equals one:\n            \n              \\[\n                 \\sin^2(x) + \\cos^2(x) = 1 % for all x\n              \\]\n    <paragraph>\n        A literal block in a table:\n    <table>\n        <tgroup cols=\"3\">\n            <colspec colwidth=\"4\">\n            <colspec colwidth=\"11\">\n            <colspec colwidth=\"4\">\n            <tbody>\n                <row>\n                    <entry>\n                        <paragraph>\n                            test\n                    <entry>\n                        <literal_block xml:space=\"preserve\">\n                            \\sin^2 x\n                    <entry>\n                        <paragraph>\n                            test\n    <paragraph>\n        A literal block in a table with auto-width columns:\n    <table classes=\"colwidths-auto\">\n        <tgroup cols=\"3\">\n            <colspec colwidth=\"4\">\n            <colspec colwidth=\"11\">\n            <colspec colwidth=\"4\">\n            <tbody>\n                <row>\n                    <entry>\n                        <paragraph>\n                            test\n                    <entry>\n                        <literal_block xml:space=\"preserve\">\n                            \\sin^2 x\n                    <entry>\n                        <paragraph>\n                            test\n    <note>\n        <paragraph>\n            A literal block in an admonition:\n        <literal_block xml:space=\"preserve\">\n            \\sin^2 x\n    <sidebar>\n        <title>\n            Literal Block in a Sidebar\n        <literal_block xml:space=\"preserve\">\n            \\sin^2 x\n    <paragraph>\n        Parsed literal block with inline markup and leading whitespace:\n    <literal_block xml:space=\"preserve\">\n           \n        <emphasis>\n            emphasis\n        , \n        <strong>\n            strong emphasis\n        , \n        <literal>\n            inline literals\n        ,\n        standalone hyperlinks (\n        <reference refuri=\"http://www.python.org\">\n            http://www.python.org\n        ),\n        <reference name=\"internal\" refid=\"internal\">\n            internal\n         and \n        <reference name=\"external\" refuri=\"http://www.python.org/\">\n            external\n         hyperlinks,\n        <target ids=\"internal\" names=\"internal\">\n            internal\n         hyperlink targets,\n        images via substitution references (\n        <image alt=\"EXAMPLE\" uri=\"../../../docs/user/rst/images/biohazard.png\">\n        ),\n        footnote references \n        <footnote_reference auto=\"*\" ids=\"footnote-reference-1\" refid=\"footnote-1\">\n            *\n        ,\n        citation references (\n        <citation_reference ids=\"citation-reference-1\" refid=\"cit2002\">\n            CIT2002\n        ), and more.\n        \n           Here are some explicit interpreted text roles:\n        a PEP reference (\n        <reference refuri=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0287\">\n            PEP 287\n        ),\n        an RFC reference (\n        <reference refuri=\"https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2822.html\">\n            RFC 2822\n        ),\n        an abbreviation (\n        <abbreviation>\n            abb.\n        ), an acronym (\n        <acronym>\n            reST\n        ),\n        code (\n        <literal classes=\"code\">\n            print \"hello world\"\n        ),\n        maths \n        <math>\n            \\sin^2(x)\n        ,\n        <subscript>\n            subscript\n         and \n        <superscript>\n            superscript\n        ,\n        <inline classes=\"custom\">\n            custom\n         \n        <inline classes=\"custom-role\">\n            roles\n        , and explicit roles for\n        <title_reference>\n            Docutils\n        ' \n        <emphasis>\n            standard\n         \n        <strong>\n            inline\n         \n        <literal>\n            markup\n        .\n    <footnote auto=\"*\" backrefs=\"footnote-reference-1\" ids=\"footnote-1\">\n        <label>\n            *\n        <paragraph>\n            This footnote is referenced in a \n            <title_reference>\n                parsed literal\n             block.\n        <paragraph>\n            It contains a literal block:\n        <literal_block xml:space=\"preserve\">\n            \\sin^2 x\n    <citation backrefs=\"citation-reference-1\" ids=\"cit2002\" names=\"cit2002\">\n        <label>\n            CIT2002\n        <paragraph>\n            Sample Citation, 2017.\n    <target ids=\"external\" names=\"external\" refuri=\"http://www.python.org/\">\n    <substitution_definition names=\"EXAMPLE\">\n        <image alt=\"EXAMPLE\" uri=\"../../../docs/user/rst/images/biohazard.png\">\n"
